<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antwerp</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antwerp is a port city in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> that was the leading commercial centre of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> in the early sixteenth century. The Portuguese crown used it as the main European market for its Asian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a>. It was a key link between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>'s trade and European finance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antwerp.jpg" alt="Antwerp" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LBM1948 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amberes;_vistas_MAS_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
